type: flow_analysis
title: Settings whitelist audit - current state analysis
key_insights[10]: "Broad patterns like Bash(bash:*), Bash(sh:*), Bash(zsh:*), Bash(python3:*) are DANGEROUS - allow arbitrary code execution","Bash(curl:*) allows POST/upload - should NOT be whitelisted broadly","Bash(osascript:*) allows AppleScript which can do anything - DANGEROUS","Bash(fnm:*) and Bash(uv:*) include install/uninstall ops - need specific read-only subcommands","Bash(gh:*) is too broad - main already has specific gh read patterns","Bash(brew cleanup:*) is DESTRUCTIVE - removes cached downloads","Bash(dotfiles add:*) is a WRITE operation",claude-mem MCP entries are stale (plugin removed),"ghostty + subcommands are ALL read-only: +version, +help, +list-fonts, +list-keybinds, +list-themes, +list-actions, +show-config","Settings use two syntaxes: 'Bash(cmd *)' (space) and 'Bash(cmd:*)' (colon) - both work"
findings[8]: "settings.json has 129 allow entries, well-organized read-only commands","settings.local.json has 170 allow entries, mix of useful tools and session cruft","12 MCP entries in local: 6 code-mode, 1 ide, 4 claude-mem (STALE - plugin removed), 1 oracle",19 WebFetch domain entries in local,"3 Skill entries in local: apple-notes, apple-reminders, dotfiles-update","65+ entries identified as one-off session cruft (loop constructs, security investigation commands, disk space one-liners)","12 local Bash entries are semantic duplicates of main (cat, echo, ls, ps, etc with colon syntax)","6 local entries exactly covered by main wildcard patterns (diskutil list, dotfiles diff/ls-files/status, echo wifi, git rev-parse)"
refs[2]: "/Users/v/.claude/settings.json - 129 allow entries, hooks, plugins, sandbox config","/Users/v/.claude/settings.local.json - 170 allow entries, no hooks/plugins"
